/*
  SINGLE-FILE VERSION, language dialect_CH (generated by tools/bundle_firmware.py):
  folder Wordclock_dialect_CH/ with Wordclock_dialect_CH.ino (settings from config.h further down) and wordclock_bundle.h (all C++ files).
  The folder name must stay the same as the .ino name (Arduino IDE).

  Wordclock.ino - Wordclock 16x16, Arduino variant, multi-language, v1.0
  Arduino variant without Home Assistant: configuration completely via the web interface
  (source webpage.html, packed into webpage.h by tools/make_webpage.py).
  Language and hardware: config.h. Fits the case from models/ (same grid, same LED layout).

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  REQUIREMENTS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. ESP32 board package by Espressif (version 2.0.x or 3.x)
     https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32
     Board manager URL: https://espressif.github.io/arduino-esp32/package_esp32_index.json
     Board: "WEMOS D1 MINI ESP32", Partition Scheme: "Default 4MB with spiffs" (no firmware update over Wi-Fi, upload via USB)
     ESP32-C6 (SuperMini / XIAO): board package 3.x only, board "ESP32C6 Dev Module" (or "XIAO_ESP32C6"),
     "USB CDC On Boot: Enabled" (serial monitor via USB). LED_PIN: GPIO2 on all boards (config.h)
  2. Only with board package 2.0.x: Adafruit NeoPixel (library manager: "Adafruit NeoPixel")
     https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_NeoPixel
     With board package 3.x no additional library is needed (LED output via the built-in RMT driver).
  Already part of the ESP32 board package, nothing to install:
     WiFi, WebServer, DNSServer, ESPmDNS, Preferences

  Folder structure (the sketch folder must be called "Wordclock"):
     Wordclock/Wordclock.ino
     Wordclock/config.h          <- language and hardware
     Wordclock/webpage.h         web interface, gzip-packed (generated from webpage.html by tools/make_webpage.py)
     Wordclock/webpage.html      source of the web interface (not compiled)
     Wordclock/wc_ui_en.h        English web interface as alternative (texts of src/wc_lang_GB.h)
     Wordclock/src/wc_core.h     shared core (also used by ESPHome)
     Wordclock/src/wc_effects.h  effect register (also used by ESPHome)
     Wordclock/src/wc_text.h     text ticker, wc_font16.h its font (also used by ESPHome)
     Wordclock/src/wc_lang_XX.h  language files (also used by ESPHome)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FEATURES
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Time words with single minutes ("+ 1 MINUTE", "+ 2..4 MINUTES"), colours per display (palette, random
    every hour, custom colour)
  - Brightness day/night, night mode by sun position (with offset), fixed times or mixed
    (sun position, but night not before / not after a set time)
  - Effects always run with at least 10 % brightness (also at night with 0 % or with the clock switched off)
  - Effects from src/wc_effects.h (rainbow, aurora, matrix, fire, confetti, stars, blink), duration and blink cycle
  - Text ticker from src/wc_text.h: a text runs letter by letter over the whole matrix (web interface and HTTP)
  - Current limit (estimate from all colour values)
  - NTP server automatically via DHCP (fallback server adjustable) or fixed, time zone selectable
  - No known Wi-Fi or Wi-Fi not found: open hotspot (name from the language file) with captive portal
    (http://192.168.4.1). The clock keeps trying to reach the saved Wi-Fi and then switches the hotspot off.
  - Until the time is known the extra words (easter egg) are shown instead of the prefix; while the hotspot is
    active they pulse blue
  - Reachable at http://<name>.local (name from the language file, adjustable) or via the IP address
  - Outdoor temperature optionally from Open-Meteo (free, no key, plain HTTP, uses the location; can be switched off in the
    web interface, a value set via HTTP has priority)
  - Control via HTTP (no Home Assistant needed), GET or POST on /api/set, several parameters combinable.
    Parameter names are the same in all languages:
      Measured values (expire after the set time, 0 = never):
        tout, tin (degC), akku (0-100), luft (0/1), alarm (0/1)
      Saved permanently:
        on (0/1), brday (1-100), brnight (0-100),
        col_time, col_vent, col_alarm, col_battery = warmwhite|white|red|orange|yellow|green|blue|violet|random|rrggbb
                                                       (col_time also "pride": one random colour per word)
        col_tempout, col_tempin = as above, but temp instead of random
        col_vent, col_alarm, col_battery, col_tempout, col_tempin also "off" = display switched off
        show_minutes, show_extra (0/1),
        show_temp, show_vent, show_alarm, show_battery (0/1, compatibility: 0 = colour "off", 1 = default colour if off)
        fxdur (0-120 s), fxcycle (0.3-3.0 s)
      Only for the effect duration:
        fx = rainbow|aurora|matrix|fire|confetti|stars|blink|stop (list: WC_FX in src/wc_effects.h)
        fxcolor = palette name or rrggbb (only for effects with colour, e.g. blink; default blue)
      Text ticker (every letter as large as the whole matrix, runs for the effect duration, at least once):
        text = text to show (UTF-8, max. 64 characters, saved), starts the ticker at once
        textstart = 1 starts the saved text again, textstart = 0 or fx=stop stops it
        textcolor = palette name, rrggbb or rainbow (only for this run; default: colour of the time,
                    with "random" every letter in the next rainbow colour)
    Example: http://wortuhr.local/api/set?brday=40&col_time=random&fx=blink&fxcolor=ff8800
    Answer: {"ok":true,"applied":[...],"ignored":[...]}; GET /api/get returns all controllable values.
    Current limit, Wi-Fi, device name, NTP, time zone, location, night mode, wiring, restart,
    factory reset only via the web interface.
*/

